		{"id":"322e093f7e7599a2","type":"text","text":"### Strengths\n\n- **Excellent extraction** – Turning papers into structured data is where Elicit shines\n- **Research workflows** – Designed for ongoing projects, not one-off searches\n- **Citation quality** – Every claim links to source papers\n- **Zotero integration** – Easy export to reference managers\n\n### Limitations\n\n- **Credits run out** – The free tier is one-time; heavy users need paid plans\n- **Not comprehensive** – A 2025 Cochrane review found Elicit lacks sensitivity for systematic searches\n- **Limited synthesis** – Better at extraction than cross-paper analysis\n\n### Pricing\n\n- **Free**: 5,000 one-time credits\n- **Plus**: $12/month (50 PDF extractions)\n- **Pro**: $49/month (200 extractions, systematic review tools)\n\nElicit, developed by Ought, has over 2 million researcher users. It's designed to help you find papers and pull structured data from them.\n\n### Core Features\n\n**Semantic search** – Search by concept, not just keywords. \"Papers about improving LLM reasoning\" finds relevant work even without exact term matches.\n\n**Data extraction** – Create columns for sample size, methodology, findings, limitations. Elicit extracts this from papers automatically.\n\n**Abstract summaries** – Quick AI summaries help you decide what's worth reading.\n\n**Workflow automation** – Save searches, export to Zotero, track papers across projects.\n\nsimple scientific and academic paper research free, extended 49 USD\n\nexport to Zotero, plus accounts, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YAiH5F-QUH4","x":1509,"y":-1075,"width":440,"height":120},
		{"id":"4857483de47026f2","type":"text","text":"Search and analyze peer-reviewed literature. Consensus draws on 250M+ research papers, including licensed full text content from leading publishers.","x":468,"y":-920,"width":645,"height":240},
